# BuildKit ignore file for lotel/Dockerfile (used instead of a context-root
# .dockerignore; the context is the repo's PARENT dir — `docker build -f
# lotel/Dockerfile ..`). Patterns are relative to that context root.
#
# The build compiles exactly two trees: lotel/ and capped/. Everything else
# — sibling projects, gigabytes of build output, and the .git internals
# cmake doesn't need — stays on the host.

*
!lotel
!capped

# --- build outputs (every builder regenerates these from source) ----------
lotel/target/
lotel/dist/
lotel/lotel-data/
capped/build/
capped/target/
capped/duckdb_unittest_tempdir/
**/target/
**/build/
**/node_modules/

# --- host-built extension blobs: these are macOS binaries; the Linux image
# --- must fetch/verify its own (build.rs would happily embed them).
lotel/crates/lotel/extensions/

# --- git internals: lotel/.git stays (build.rs stamps --version from it);
# --- capped's build pins OVERRIDE_GIT_DESCRIBE=v2.0.0, so the vendored
# --- duckdb / ci-tools checkouts don't need their .git directories.
capped/.git/
capped/duckdb/.git/
capped/extension-ci-tools/.git/
